    { math: '3 · One-point, two-point, three-point', note: 'One vanishing point (a hallway), two (a building corner — the standard), three (looking up or down — the drama). The horizon line is ALWAYS the viewer\'s eye level — the one rule that untangles every construction.' },
    { math: '4 · Perspective is a convention, not truth', note: 'Chinese scroll painting moved the eye through space; isometric projection keeps parallels parallel (the architect\'s drawing lesson); photography revealed lens distortion perspective omits. One coherent system among several — knowing its assumptions is the mastery.' },
